e example device mappings with your own asset selections."},"14":{"id":"/docs/how-it-works-12","page_id":"/docs/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-it-works#2-map-the-payload-fields","content":"Under **Field mappings**, edit `demo-bess` using the pencil button. For your own payload, select **Add mapping** instead."},"15":{"id":"/docs/how-it-works-13","page_id":"/docs/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-it-works#2-map-the-payload-fields","content":"Choose the asset type and set **Asset ID path** to the field containing the local device ID. In the example, `device.id` identifies the device, and `measurements.soc` supplies the FlexBIT field `bess_storage_soc`."},"16":{"id":"/docs/how-it-works-14","page_id":"/docs/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-it-works#2-map-the-payload-fields","content":"Enter a payload path for each measurement you want to send, then save. Mapping changes apply without restarting the adapter."},"17":{"id":"/docs/how-it-works-15","page_id":"/docs/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-it-works#over-http","content":"Run this from the installation directory to send the BESS payload shown in the screenshots."},"18":{"id":"/docs/how-it-works-16","page_id":"/docs/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-it-works#over-http","content":"With Docker:"},"19":{"id":"/docs/how-it-works-17","page_id":"/docs/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-it-works#over-http","content":"Without Docker, use a second terminal while the adapter is running:"},"20":{"id":"/docs/how-it-works-18","page_id":"/docs/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-it-works#over-http","content":"For your own integration, POST a JSON object to `/v1/ingest` with `Content-Type: application/json` and `X-Mapping-Id` set to your mapping ID. For example:"},"21":{"id":"/docs/how-it-works-19","page_id":"/docs/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-it-works#over-http","content":"An `accepted` response means the adapter saved the event locally. Check **Events** for delivery to FlexBIT."},"22":{"id":"/docs/how-it-works-20","page_id":"/docs/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-it-works#over-mqtt","content":"Open **MQTT** and select **Add connection**. Enter your broker URL and client ID, add credentials if needed, and add a subscription pairing your telemetry topic with a mapping ID."},"23":{"id":"/docs/how-it-works-21","page_id":"/docs/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-it-works#over-mqtt","content":"For the bundled Docker broker, use `mqtt://mosquitto:1883`. For standalone mode, use the address of your external broker. A BESS subscription can use topic `devices/bess/telemetry` and mapping ID `demo-bess`."},"24":{"id":"/docs/how-it-works-22","page_id":"/docs/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-it-works#over-mqtt","content":"If you enabled MQTT during Docker installation, the local connection and demo subscriptions are already configured. With Mosquitto clients installed on the host, send a test message with:"},"25":{"id":"/docs/how-it-works-23","page_id":"/docs/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-it-works#over-mqtt","content":"For commands to a device, add a **Command target** linking its FlexBIT asset ID to an MQTT connection and topic. Check outgoing attempts on **Commands**. The current adapter accepts commands through `/internal/commands`; it does not subscribe to platform commands automatically."},"26":{"id":"/docs/how-it-works-24","page_id":"/docs/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-it-works#4-check-the-result","content":"Open **Events** and expand your event. The left side shows the incoming JSON; the right side shows the mapped FlexBIT payload and delivery state."},"27":{"id":"/docs/how-it-works-25","page_id":"/docs/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-it-works#4-check-the-result","content":"**Pending** means the event is waiting for mapping. Check its error, mapping ID, and payload paths if it stays pending."},"28":{"id":"/docs/how-it-works-26","page_id":"/docs/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-it-works#4-check-the-result","content":"**Mapped** means the payload is ready for delivery."},"29":{"id":"/docs/how-it-works-27","page_id":"/docs/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-it-works#4-check-the-result","content":"**Delivered** means the adapter sent it to FlexBIT."},"30":{"id":"/docs/how-it-works-28","page_id":"/docs/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-it-works#4-check-the-result","content":"If delivery does not complete, check the error shown on the event and verify your FlexBIT credentials and network connection."},"31":{"id":"/docs/installation","page_id":"/docs/installation","type":"page","content":"Installation","breadcrumbs":["FlexBIT Local Adapter"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/installation"},"32":{"id":"/docs/installation-0","page_id":"/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/installation","content":"Install with Docker or run the standalone adapter on Linux."},"33":{"id":"/docs/installation-1","page_id":"/docs/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/installation#get-your-flexbit-credentials","content":"Get your FlexBIT credentials"},"34":{"id":"/docs/installation-2","page_id":"/docs/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/installation#run-the-installer","content":"Run the installer"},"35":{"id":"/docs/installation-3","page_id":"/docs/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/installation#with-docker","content":"With Docker"},"36":{"id":"/docs/installation-4","page_id":"/docs/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/installation#without-docker","content":"Without Docker"},"37":{"id":"/docs/installation-5","page_id":"/docs/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/installation#open-the-dashboard","content":"Open the dashboard"},"38":{